  "extraction": "All nine declaration statements and proof bodies retained byte-for-byte. Changed import header, module comment and namespace only. Direct mathlib imports replace the ArithmeticDynamics closure; no PNT module is copied or imported.",
  "formalScope": "For natural N != 0, evaluates the full signed endpoint count E(N) by 2 E(N) = 1 + (-1)^cardFactors(N), proves E(N) is 0 or 1, and preserves the original inclusive double-sum equality. Includes divisor-pairing and convolution lemmas. The sqrt-cutoff count identity holds for all natural N.",
  "writtenConsequence": {
    "file": "building-blocks/hyperbola-endpoint.md",
    "status": "Written real sawtooth conversion, not formalized in this module.",
    "value": "For the complete outer sum 1 <= n <= N, ordinary sawtooth minus midpoint sawtooth is -(1+(-1)^Omega(N))/4, hence 0 or -1/2.",
    "restriction": "Not valid for arbitrary restricted outer blocks. N=6 and only n=1 gives count 2 and correction -1."
  },
  "mathematicalNovelty": "Classical divisor pairing and Mobius inversion. No originality claim.",
  "formalizationPriority": "No first-formalization claim.",
